ion/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e1fad6f-855e-553e-8d75-e321cc680343" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e1fad6f-855e-553e-8d75-e321cc680343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d0c098d1-7ef1-5ad1-b259-c1614202d6d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5008f77-48d1-5bb2-ba5f-fe9365aea196" "answer-d0c098d1-7ef1-5ad1-b259-c1614202d6d3" "answer-d290f871-27b8-5194-87df-869b3c3e63ff" "answer-444efbe8-dff8-5c45-a4c6-ad837d7e5d57" "answer-87e9f515-7eb3-5e62-a8a0-a8403b398027"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5008f77-48d1-5bb2-ba5f-fe9365aea196" :answer/id #uuid "b5008f77-48d1-5bb2-ba5f-fe9365aea196" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0c098d1-7ef1-5ad1-b259-c1614202d6d3" :answer/id #uuid "d0c098d1-7ef1-5ad1-b259-c1614202d6d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d290f871-27b8-5194-87df-869b3c3e63ff" :answer/id #uuid "d290f871-27b8-5194-87df-869b3c3e63ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-444efbe8-dff8-5c45-a4c6-ad837d7e5d57" :answer/id #uuid "444efbe8-dff8-5c45-a4c6-ad837d7e5d57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87e9f515-7eb3-5e62-a8a0-a8403b398027" :answer/id #uuid "87e9f515-7eb3-5e62-a8a0-a8403b398027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-99569175-b9f3-5c01-983c-724e408918e3" :question/id #uuid "99569175-b9f3-5c01-983c-724e408918e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73947" :question/problem "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ {x}^{4} \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $r\\cdot s=0$ and $x<0$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $r\\cdot s=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot {x}^{4}+0\\cdot 8+x\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ -3+2{x}^{2}+0-x & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-x-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-1)\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}-4(2)(-3)}}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{25}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1.$ Since we need $x<0$, our final answer is $x=-1$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17f4d7b6-1d54-58dd-a546-544bac478642"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17f4d7b6-1d54-58dd-a546-544bac478642" :answer-field/id #uuid "17f4d7b6-1d54-58dd-a546-544bac478642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-548a5160-ea2a-5460-be28-4daa3a49d1cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-548a5160-ea2a-5460-be28-4daa3a49d1cb" "answer-a5314088-f525-53ae-8f0e-c1cb3cc6d421" "answer-b29fdb02-3b26-5216-8f4e-13b529bbcd39" "answer-4a8a54af-e3aa-5606-a52d-b582cbbc8cca" "answer-280517df-9242-59ab-bc3e-65af0d2d37ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-548a5160-ea2a-5460-be28-4daa3a49d1cb" :answer/id #uuid "548a5160-ea2a-5460-be28-4daa3a49d1cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5314088-f525-53ae-8f0e-c1cb3cc6d421" :answer/id #uuid "a5314088-f525-53ae-8f0e-c1cb3cc6d421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b29fdb02-3b26-5216-8f4e-13b529bbcd39" :answer/id #uuid "b29fdb02-3b26-5216-8f4e-13b529bbcd39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a8a54af-e3aa-5606-a52d-b582cbbc8cca" :answer/id #uuid "4a8a54af-e3aa-5606-a52d-b582cbbc8cca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-280517df-9242-59ab-bc3e-65af0d2d37ee" :answer/id #uuid "280517df-9242-59ab-bc3e-65af0d2d37ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ac43b1b5-6764-5241-bdc0-c6b7a39ba60f" :question/id #uuid "ac43b1b5-6764-5241-bdc0-c6b7a39ba60f" :question/math-academy-id "q-35098" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k+2\\end{aligned}].$ If $u\\cdot v=0$, find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $u\\cdot v=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $k$ and then solve for $k$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ 1\\cdot k+3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-5)+6\\cdot (k+2) & =0 \\\\ k+12-10+6k+12 & =0 \\\\ 7k+14 & =0 \\\\ 7k & =-14 \\\\ k & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $k=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-513e934d-104b-54ec-9e02-0f0638cf1a17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-513e934d-104b-54ec-9e02-0f0638cf1a17" :answer-field/id #uuid "513e934d-104b-54ec-9e02-0f0638cf1a17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c75b571-33fa-5088-b2e0-5d3674cd21af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c75b571-33fa-5088-b2e0-5d3674cd21af" "answer-7337f43d-3302-55c7-837c-201949c779c0" "answer-14c7e230-fd06-52b6-a9bf-f5d1185d3530" "answer-ab52cab0-c0f9-5d04-a911-88760c863129" "answer-d6c70620-90f9-5604-afb9-68b09a4d75d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c75b571-33fa-5088-b2e0-5d3674cd21af" :answer/id #uuid "3c75b571-33fa-5088-b2e0-5d3674cd21af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7337f43d-3302-55c7-837c-201949c779c0" :answer/id #uuid "7337f43d-3302-55c7-837c-201949c779c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14c7e230-fd06-52b6-a9bf-f5d1185d3530" :answer/id #uuid "14c7e230-fd06-52b6-a9bf-f5d1185d3530" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab52cab0-c0f9-5d04-a911-88760c863129" :answer/id #uuid "ab52cab0-c0f9-5d04-a911-88760c863129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6c70620-90f9-5604-afb9-68b09a4d75d9" :answer/id #uuid "d6c70620-90f9-5604-afb9-68b09a4d75d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121062 :tutorial/content "To add two vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^n,$ we just need to add their corresponding components. To illustrate, consider the vectors $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b} \\in \\mathbb{R}^4,$ given by\n\n![](images/1f/1f1b79f2e61fccbb27944284cbdd217a311a7f795100cfbb56340a457814b407.svg)\n\nTo compute $\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b},$ all we have to do is to add each component of the vector $\\mathbf{a}$ with the corresponding component of $\\mathbf{b}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5+(-5) \\\\ 1+3 \\\\ -3+1 \\\\ 6+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can only compute the sum, difference, or dot product of two vectors if both vectors have the same number of components. For example, we can't find the following sum, so we say it's *undefined*:\n![](images/6c/6c377966aa9fa1d581c0f9e3ba16bceb4020471914d5c4fb61118ff7cd709466.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121033 :tutorial/content "In general, if we have two vectors $\\mathbf{u},\\mathbf{v}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$ and a scalar $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb{R},$ then our vector operations are defined as follows:\n\n1\\. The **sum/difference** of the two vectors is defined as\n  ![](images/fc/fc78b2f4e9262108a217e57fec67e096b8b8b18e1486bec8e51df60b8afdfdfa.svg)\n\n2\\. **Scalar multiplication** of a vector is defined as\n  ![](images/e7/e78025f3481423365b2e924b6f8ba4e59f41e0c644ced7d2263238b219cba27a.svg)\n\n3\\. The **dot product** of two vectors is defined as\n\n  $$\n  \\quad \\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v} = \\underbrace{u_1 \\cdot v_1 + u_2 \\cdot v_2 + \\cdots + u_n \\cdot v_n}_{\\Large{n} \\,\\textrm{-terms}} = \\sum_{i=1}^n u_i v_i.\n  $$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-2af09a21-2c9f-5742-9701-8495f499a998" :question/id #uuid "2af09a21-2c9f-5742-9701-8495f499a998"] ["question-2af09a21-2c9f-5742-9701-8495f499a998" :question/math-academy-id "q-105095"] ["question-2af09a21-2c9f-5742-9701-8495f499a998" :question/problem "Let $b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find $-\\frac{1}{2}b.$"] ["question-2af09a21-2c9f-5742-9701-8495f499a998" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $b$ by $-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}b & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-2af09a21-2c9f-5742-9701-8495f499a998" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-d15c7edc-ea7c-583c-aafa-9f4f9a26bd10" :answer-field/id #uuid "d15c7edc-ea7c-583c-aafa-9f4f9a26bd10"] ["answer-310ef4de-eb23-5d04-80bc-bd56d0cdf937" :answer/id #uuid "310ef4de-eb23-5d04-80bc-bd56d0cdf937"] ["answer-310ef4de-eb23-5d04-80bc-bd56d0cdf937" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-310ef4de-eb23-5d04-80bc-bd56d0cdf937" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{ali